node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
# Everything retrace generates lives under .retrace/ — run dirs, diff images,
# repro bundles — and none of it belongs in a commit. Ignore the directory's
# contents wholesale rather than naming each subdir as it is added, so a new
# generated location is covered the day it appears.
#
# The `.retrace/*` form matters: git cannot re-include a path whose PARENT
# directory is excluded, so a blanket `.retrace/` would make the negation
# below dead. Ignoring the entries instead leaves the directory itself
# traversable.
#
# The recording team key is a secret: it comes from RETRACE_RECORDING_KEY or
# .retrace/recording.key, and must never be committed. It is covered here.
.retrace/*
# ...except the machine-owned wire-rule overlay, which IS committed — it is
# the reviewed record of which fields are allowed to vary (config.OverlayPath).
!.retrace/wire-rules.json
#
# Reference bundles ARE committed — .retrace-ref/<app>/<flow>/reference is
# the blessed artifact a diff runs against, and an ignored bundle is a diff
# that silently has nothing to compare against on a fresh clone. There is
# deliberately NO pattern for it here: it lives OUTSIDE .retrace/ precisely
# so the blanket rule above cannot swallow it. Do not "tidy" the two roots
# into one. The repro bundles `retrace ref reject` emits are the opposite —
# throwaway attachments for a bug report — and land under .retrace/repro/,
# which line 17 already covers; naming it explicitly would contradict the
# wholesale rule stated above, so it is not named.
coverage/
# Root-anchored: a bare `bin/` also matches adapters/maestro/bin/, an npm
# package's tracked bin directory (Task 17) — not a build-output dir at all.
/bin/

# `ensemble up`'s own run-time state (hop log, build staleness stamps, pid
# files) — generated fresh by every run, wherever ensemble.yaml lives.
.ensemble/

# Building an ensemble/retrace CLI directly from inside its module dir
# (`cd ensemble && go build ./cmd/ensemble`) drops an extensionless binary
# named after the built package, right there — distinct from the repo-root
# `./ensemble`/`./retrace` binaries `make build`/`go build -o` produce,
# which land outside these module dirs and are each dev's own choice to
# leave uncommitted.
/ensemble/ensemble
/retrace/retrace

# sample/ Go services are standalone modules (not part of go.work); `go
# build -o <name> .` in each one drops an extensionless binary named after
# the module right next to main.go (see each one's build: in ensemble.yaml).
sample/services/*/catalog-svc
sample/services/*/edge-gw
sample/services/*/notify-worker
# notify-worker's simulated "sent notifications" log — regenerated every run.
sample/services/notify-worker/notifications.log
# order-svc is a standalone Gradle project (also not part of go.work, and
# not a Go module at all) — its build output and Gradle's local cache.
sample/services/order-svc/build/
sample/services/order-svc/.gradle/

# web-app's Playwright run output — regenerated every `npm test`.
sample/clients/web-app/test-results/
sample/clients/web-app/playwright-report/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledgers, briefs, reports, review
# packages. Local coordination state, never part of the source tree.
.superpowers/

# Dashboard build output is embedded via go:embed (ensemble/server/ui/ui.go).
# Only the placeholder ensemble/server/ui/dist/index.html is committed — the
# blanket `dist/` rule above would otherwise swallow it too, so unignore
# this dist/ specifically and its index.html, then re-ignore the built
# assets/ subtree (plus the favicon files Vite copies from ensemble-ui/public/
# verbatim — those live tracked at their public/ source, not here).
# `pnpm -r build` overwrites index.html locally with the real bundle, which
# must never land in a commit — `git restore
# ensemble/server/ui/dist/index.html` after building, before committing.
!ensemble/server/ui/dist/
!ensemble/server/ui/dist/index.html
ensemble/server/ui/dist/assets/
ensemble/server/ui/dist/favicon.svg
ensemble/server/ui/dist/favicon.ico
ensemble/server/ui/dist/apple-touch-icon.png

# Same hazard as ensemble/server/ui/dist, one binary over: retrace's review
# UI is embedded via go:embed (retrace/serve/ui/ui.go), only the placeholder
# retrace/serve/ui/dist/index.html is committed, and the blanket `dist/` rule
# at the top would otherwise swallow it. `pnpm -r build` overwrites it with
# the real bundle, which must never land in a commit — `git restore
# retrace/serve/ui/dist/index.html` after building, before committing.
!retrace/serve/ui/dist/
!retrace/serve/ui/dist/index.html
retrace/serve/ui/dist/assets/
